I present here the comparison of temperature and PM2.5 measurements made with  our sensors and with two EPA Air Quality Sensors: one located in Dudley Square, Roxbury, and the second one located in Von Hillern St.  


\section{Temperature}\label{sec:temperature_results}
\subsection{Temp---Summary of $RMSE$ and correlation coefficients.}

Figure \ref{fig:rmse_temp} shows the $RMSE$ values obtained for temperature, computed across all our sensors. Carter (ref) refers to Amy Mueller's team sensor which we had used for reference in previous stages of the project.  

\begin{figure}[H]
    \centering
    \includegraphics[width = \linewidth]{Figures/temp_09_rmse.png}
    \caption{$RMSE$ temperature values when comparing measurements from our sensors with those of the EPA Air Quality Sensors.}
    \label{fig:rmse_temp}
\end{figure}


Figure \ref{fig:coeffs_temp} shows the correlation coefficients between the temperature measurements of our sensors and those made with the EPA Air Quality Sensors. 

\begin{figure}[H]
    \centering
    \includegraphics[width = \linewidth]{Figures/temp_10_corr.png}
    \caption{Correlation coefficients obtained between our sensors and the 2 reference AQS.}
    \label{fig:coeffs_temp}
\end{figure}

